  {
    "id": "6017d084e26f20d9793452ab",
    "path": "parquet::file::properties::CdcOptions::max_chunk_size",
    "name": "max_chunk_size",
    "owner": "parquet::file::properties::CdcOptions",
    "crate": "parquet",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "struct_field",
    "signature": "max_chunk_size: usize",
    "docs": "Maximum chunk size in bytes, default is 1024 KiB.\nThe chunker will create a new chunk whenever the chunk size exceeds this value.\nNote that the parquet writer has a related [`data_page_size_limit`] property that\ncontrols the maximum size of a parquet data page after encoding. While setting\n`data_page_size_limit` to a smaller value than `max_chunk_size` doesn't affect\nthe chunking effectiveness, it results in more small parquet data pages.\n\n[`data_page_size_limit`]: WriterPropertiesBuilder::set_data_page_size_limit",
