  {
    "id": "96e659b8a6925a948507144a",
    "path": "parquet::file::properties::CdcOptions::norm_level",
    "name": "norm_level",
    "owner": "parquet::file::properties::CdcOptions",
    "crate": "parquet",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "struct_field",
    "signature": "norm_level: i32",
    "docs": "Number of bit adjustment to the gearhash mask in order to center the chunk size\naround the average size more aggressively, default is 0.\nIncreasing the normalization level increases the probability of finding a chunk,\nimproving the deduplication ratio, but also increasing the number of small chunks\nresulting in many small parquet data pages. The default value provides a good\nbalance between deduplication ratio and fragmentation.\nUse norm_level=1 or norm_level=2 to reach a higher deduplication ratio at the\nexpense of fragmentation. Negative values can also be used to reduce the\nprobability of finding a chunk, resulting in larger chunks and fewer data pages.\nNote that values outside [-3, 3] are not recommended, prefer using the default\nvalue of 0 for most use cases.",
    "span": {
